    "q-5891": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5891",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The table below defines the function $f(x).$ Is the function even, odd, or neither?\n\n| **$x$** | $-99$ | $-52$ | $-8$ | $8$ | $52$ | $99$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $150$ | $70$ | $0$ | $-11$ | $-92$ | $-180$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n- a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain of $f$\n\n- a function is odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain of $f$\n\nFirst, we have\n\n$$\nf(-99)=150\\ne f(99).\n$$\n\nThis means that $f(-x)\\ne f(x)$ at least for some values of $x$ in the domain of the function. So, the function is not even.\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\nf(-99)=150\\ne -f(99).\n$$\n\nThis means that $f(-x)\\ne -f(x)$ at least for some values of $x$ in the domain of the function. So, the function is not odd.\n\nHence, the function is neither even nor odd.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
